Derived files
-------------

device/apps/claude_buddy.py
    Adapted from buddy/device/apps/claude_buddy.py. The local change is
    transport selection: the BLE peripheral can be swapped for the USB-serial
    link in device/buddy_serial.py.

host/buddy_deploy.py (push_file)
    Lineage rather than code. It began as a reimplementation of
    buddy/scripts/push.py, whose paste-mode plus base64 transfer mechanism was
    upstream's; that mechanism has since been replaced wholesale by mpremote's
    raw-paste transport, and what remains — the install layout, the
    post-transfer stat — is local. Recorded because the derivation is real
    history, not because upstream code survives in it. It lived in
    host/buddy_push.py until that module was folded into host/buddy_deploy.py.

The peer modules the device imports at runtime (buddy_protocol.py,
buddy_ui_cp.py, buddy_state.py, buddy_chars.py, main.py) are used unmodified
and are not redistributed here — they are installed onto the device's flash by
the m5-onboard skill from the upstream clone. host/buddy_deploy.py reads them
off the device to compile them, and keeps the copy it read under vendor/,
which is untracked.
